WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.760
All right. Anything in my teeth?

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:08.640
As a former professor who taught entrepreneurship, I often get asked:

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.300
"What are the secrets to good leadership?"

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:17.300
Here's one piece of advice: Be nice! Now,
niceness might seem like a naive

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:21.570
strategy, especially in this climate. It
feels like our society today has become

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:26.010
a battle of competing pessimisms.
Wouldn't an actively nice leader seem

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:32.550
out of place? But that's exactly the
point! These days, warm heartedness is

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:38.790
radical and unexpected... and it turns out,
also very effective. In one 2013 study,

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:43.950
researchers found that a positive kind
leader is judged to be 132 percent more

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:48.570
effective than an unpleasant leader. Now,
niceness does not mean we need fewer

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:52.829
disagreements – or less debate. Business
and policy require a healthy competition

00:00:52.829 --> 00:00:57.660
of ideas. But our intellectual contest
should be fierce and friendly at the

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:05.080
same time. So leaders: Get nice! It will
help you build a sustainable success and a better world!

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.760
To learn more about the
competitive advantage of being nice,

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:14.430
click the links in the description below.
Also, let us know what other topics you

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:18.680
want AEI scholars to cover in 60 seconds.

